Figure~\ref{fig:real} shows that on seen tasks LLM-backbone methods outperform RT-1 and Diffusion Policy, with UP-VLA best (0.80, versus 0.75 for UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu and 0.65 for UP-VLA-RT-2). On unseen-object grasping, the semantic variant UP-VLA-RT-2 (0.50) beats UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu (0.30), and UP-VLA is highest (0.60), consistent with MMU supplying semantics that actions can exploit. On precise tasks the order reverses between the two variants (0.35 for the prediction-only model versus 0.20 for RT-2-style), and UP-VLA reaches 0.55, indicating that future prediction contributes spatial detail. Thus the two objectives help on complementary axes and the combination is best on all three.

